.venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
# Matches the live cache AND every dated backup beside it (e.g.
# .provenance_cache.pre-2026-07-25/). The bare `.provenance_cache/` rule did not,
# so a `git add -A` would have committed a stale evidence pool that check_claims.py
# could later read by mistake.
.provenance_cache*/

# permutation_design.py block checkpoints: raw per-replicate scores, regenerable.
.permutation_design_cache/

# Derived state -- regenerate with status.py. Never commit; that is how state becomes stale history.
STATUS.json
